course: dictionary
lesson: 9712
title: Words for how a land is ruled
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sultanate is a land ruled by a sultan. A sultan is a Muslim king or ruler, so when you see sultanate, look for clues about who is in charge. «In 1337 the Delhi Sultanate ruled much of north India.» The word ruled is your clue: a sultanate is a country or land with a sultan in charge.
explain: Sultanate can also mean the time when a sultan ruled, or the sultan's position. Read the whole sentence to see which meaning fits. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Be careful: a sultanate may be from the past. «If you played Europa Universalis 5, you saw a different map in 1337» shows that today's countries grew out of older states like the Delhi Sultanate. When context is not enough, a dictionary or a teacher can settle it.
fact: A sultanate is a country or land ruled by a sultan.
fact: A sultan is a Muslim king or ruler.
fact: «The Delhi Sultanate ruled much of north India» in 1337.
fact: Sultanate can also mean the time when a sultan ruled, or the sultan's position.
fact: Brunei and the Sultanate of Oman are sultanates today.
exercise: «In 1337 the Delhi Sultanate ruled much of north India.» What is a sultanate? | A type of food | A large river in India | A group of people who sing | *A country or land ruled by a sultan
exercise: «Persian was used at the courts of the Delhi Sultanate and the Mughals.» A court belongs to a ruler. Who would hold a court in a sultanate? | A school teacher | A shop owner | *A sultan | A football coach
exercise: Sultan means a Muslim king or ruler. Which word is closest in meaning? | Pilot | *King | Baker | Farmer
test: What is a sultan? | *A Muslim king or ruler | A school teacher | A type of boat | A kind of fish
test: Which meaning of sultanate fits «He was proud of the sultanate's long history»? | A grassy field | *The land ruled by a sultan, or the time a sultan ruled | A kind of song | A small village by the coast
exam: Which place is a sultanate today, according to the facts above? | Mongolia | Egypt | *Brunei | Paris
